# Tracer: introduce an atomic prop fact whose complete meaning is one existential.
#
# Before (did not work):
# witness $divides(6, 2) from 3:
#     6 = 2 * 3
# Former implementation name: this statement was represented by
# `WitnessNamedExistFact`.
#
# Now (verified): it is represented by `WitnessAtomicFact`; the parser retains
# only the atomic fact, and execution resolves
# its current concrete definition before checking the supplied witness.

prop divides(p Z, u Z):
    exist k Z st {p = u * k}

witness $divides(6, 2) from 3:
    6 = 2 * 3

$divides(6, 2)
obtain divisor_witness from $divides(6, 2)
6 = 2 * divisor_witness

# Boundary: `exist!` is covered by `witness_atomic_exist_unique_fact.lit`.
# `not exist`, abstract props, nonexistential definitions, and definitions with
# multiple clauses remain rejected.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/01_proof_patterns/witness_atomic_fact.lit
